target/
**/target/
# The Dockerfile packages a pre-built binary and its license notices from
# target/<TARGETARCH>/release/, so those files stay in the build context while the rest of target/
# is excluded. For a local build, stage them from the paths cargo and cargo-about write, e.g. on
# x86_64:
#   mkdir -p target/amd64/release
#   cp target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/cni-config target/amd64/release/
!target/*/release/cni-config
!target/*/release/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES
!target/*/release/COPYRIGHT-rust-std.html
!target/*/release/COPYRIGHT-musl
